ess, I recommend we explore some relaxation techniques that can help calm your mind and body. One technique that might be helpful is progressive muscle relaxation. This involves tensing and relaxing different muscle groups in your body, starting with your toes and moving up to your head. We can also explore some cognitive-behavioral therapy (CBT) techniques, such as reframing negative thoughts and challenging distorted or unhelpful thinking patterns.\n\nIn addition to these techniques, I'd like to encourage you to prioritize self-care activities that bring you joy and help you unwind. This might include activities like reading, taking a walk, or practicing yoga. It's essential to make time for these activities, even if it's just 15-20 minutes a day, to help you recharge and reduce feelings of burnout.\n\nBefore we proceed, I want to check in with you about your current risk level. On a scale of 1-10, with 1 being minimal risk and 10 being high risk, how would you rate your emotional state right now? This will help me better understand your needs and ensure we're taking the necessary steps to prioritize your well-being.\n\nRemember, our goal is to work together to reduce your workload, increase your self-care activities, and improve your sleep quality. We'll take things one step at a time, and I'll be here to support you every step of the way.\n\nHow does that sound? Is there anything specific you'd like to focus on or any concerns you'd like to address before we move forward?","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"overwhelmed","progressIndicators":["reduced workload","increased self-care activities","improved sleep quality"],"recommendedApproach":"cognitive-behavioral therapy with relaxation techniques","riskLevel":2,"themes":["work-related stress","burnout"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"overwhelmed","riskLevel":2}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-08T20:20:30.430Z"},{"_id":"69adda32d2a07c46a2e90e1f","content":"ok thank you","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-03-08T20:21:06.240Z"},{"_id":"69adda32d2a07c46a2e90e20","content":"It sounds like you're feeling a bit neutral at the moment, and that's completely okay. I'm here to listen and support you without any judgment. Since we're just starting our conversation, I'd like to get to know you a bit better and understand what brings you here today. Can you tell me a little more about what's been on your mind lately, or is there something specific that you're hoping to talk about or work through? I'm here to listen and help in any way I can.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"neutral","progressIndicators":["user engagement","response brevity"],"recommendedApproach":"open-ended questioning","riskLevel":0,"themes":[]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"neutral","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-03-08T20:21:06.241Z"}],"memory":{"sessionContext":{"conversationThemes":[],"currentTechnique":null},"userProfile":{"emotionalState":[],"preferences":{},"riskLevel":0}},"message":"are there any specific techniques to deal with anxiety","systemPrompt":"You are an AI therapist assistant. Your role is to:\n        1. Provide empathetic and supportive responses\n        2. Use evidence-based therapeutic techniques\n        3. Maintain professional boundaries\n        4. Monitor for risk factors\n        5. Guide users toward their therapeutic goals\n        \n        IMPORTANT: Keep responses concise and conversational.\n        - Maximum 3-4 short sentences per response\n        - Ask one follow-up question to keep the conversation going\n        - Avoid long paragraphs\n        - Be warm but brief, like a real therapy conversation"},"name":"therapy/session.message"},"level":"info","message":"Sending message to Inngest:","timestamp":"2026-03-08T20:25:56.415Z"}
